# Graphify Architectural Context Rule

Before designing features or refactoring cross-module code:
1. Check if `graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md` or `graphify-out/wiki/index.md` exists.
2. Review God Nodes and surprising connections in `GRAPH_REPORT.md` to prevent unintended regressions across modules.
3. For multi-module questions, run `/graphify query "<question>"` or `/graphify path "<from>" "<to>"` to trace call paths.
4. Keep the knowledge graph fresh using `/graphify . --update` or after major commits.

## Project truth

This template uses a lightweight WWG-inspired project-truth layer:

- Read `.project-truth/truth/project-truth-summary.md` and `.project-truth/workspace/current-task.md` before meaningful work.
- Treat `.project-truth/truth/` as canonical accepted product and architecture truth.
- Treat `.project-truth/workspace/` as agent context, not a competing source of truth.
- Treat `.project-truth/governance/` and reports as drift/verification guidance and evidence.
- Synchronize durable discoveries back into canonical truth before closeout.

## Existing application adoption

When the user says `adopt` or `/adopt`, follow the evidence-first `app/`
baseline workflow in `AGENTS.md`: inspect relevant files, record a dated report
in `.project-truth/reports/`, and promote only confirmed findings to canonical
truth. Never modify application source or invent unknown product facts.
